    <div style="padding-top:16px">
      <p style="font-size:15px; line-height:26px; margin:0; max-width:78ch">A <strong>package index</strong> is the phone book grim searches: pointers into your registries, not another copy of the packages. The public one is the default, not the system — one command scaffolds your own, and your forge's Pages serves it.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="padding-top:14px">
      <div data-cmd style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:11.2px; padding:2px 0">
        <pre style="flex:1; min-width:0; font-size:13.5px; line-height:30px"><span style="color:var(--color-accent)">$ </span>npx @grimoire-rs/indexer init<span class="dim">                    # scaffold the index repo</span></pre>
        <button type="button" class="cmd-copy" data-copy="npx @grimoire-rs/indexer init">copy</button>
      </div>
      <div data-cmd style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:11.2px; padding:2px 0">
        <pre style="flex:1; min-width:0; font-size:13.5px; line-height:30px"><span style="color:var(--color-accent)">$ </span>git push<span class="dim">                                         # Pages builds and serves it</span></pre>
        <button type="button" class="cmd-copy" data-copy="git push">copy</button>
      </div>
      <div data-cmd style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:11.2px; padding:2px 0">
        <pre style="flex:1; min-width:0; font-size:13.5px; line-height:30px"><span style="color:var(--color-accent)">$ </span>grim config registry add acme --index https://acme.github.io/index</pre>
        <button type="button" class="cmd-copy" data-copy="grim config registry add acme --index https://acme.github.io/index">copy</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fanout" style="padding-top:22px; align-items:start">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">what you get</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px; line-height:26px; margin:0; color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 74%, transparent)">A searchable catalog site and the JSON grim resolves against, plus a contribution gate that refuses a pull request writing a namespace its author does not own. Publishers announce into it with <span class="mono">grim publish --announce</span>.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">what you run</p>
        <p style="font-size:15px; line-height:26px; margin:0; color:color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 74%, transparent)">Nothing. No index server, no database, no account — a repository on the forge you already use, private or public. <a href="/start.html">Walk through it, step by step →</a></p>
      </div>
